      "output": "**Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS (engineering scope).** Full report at `runs/mw_protocol_v3_v1_1_sources_review_20260913/reviewer_scratch/C03_review_report.md`, with all harnesses and logs alongside it. Owner decides acceptance.\n\n**What was verified** (all against the frozen scope — 267/267 snapshot files hash-verified, live repo identical, still identical after the review; original MG-K10 DOCX re-hashed and matching `7302…4199`):\n\n- **Claim 1 (DOCX projection)** — my own ZIP/XML walk vs `parse_docx` on the real document: all 2,608 blocks resolve to real XML elements; 22/22 tables with identical locator sets; all 5 nested tables retained; gridSpan 32/32 and vMerge 40/40 exactly matching XML ground truth; exact per-character text coverage (86,696 == 86,696); headers/footers as roles; real hash binding; deterministic; visual/tracked-change/coverage semantics as claimed.\n- **Claim 2 (identity service)** — 27/27 independent challenges, including a genuine non-monkeypatch post-staging SQL failure (rogue duplicate `domain_event_id`): current unchanged, staging retained, retry/unrelated keys unaffected; filesystem-latest never becomes current; tamper detected loudly; replay preserves successor; relabel attempts on any historical record rejected.\n- **Claim 3 (mounted API)** — disabled mount has zero side effects; enabled-without-db fails closed; admission gate rejects non-admitted projects with the Chinese envelope before any write; POST/list/parse/download all work with byte-exact download; invalid DOCX (three variants) → 400 Chinese explanation, nothing adopted; invalid role → 422 in the same envelope; store path is `<full-db-filename>.artifacts`, created lazily; node client tests 3/3 (FormData boundary left to browser).\n- **Claim 4 (seed compiler)** — 30/30 adversarial challenges: per-(source, locator) exact quote binding; spliced/fabricated quotes rejected; competitor/company roles stay `reference_only` even with perfect body quotes; multi-dose retained as proposals; canonical always empty; missing explicit.\n- **Claim 5 (sizing)** — on the real document: 2,586 units, 511,934-byte payload, unit text exactly equals leaf text (no truncation, no cap), zero units carry joined row text, row/cell coordinates explicit, ~355k chars avoided vs naive row-repeat, every unit locator XML-traceable, no model call and no budget claim.\n- **Declared targets** — 25 pytest + 3 node tests all pass (logs in scratch).\n\n**The one condition (F-1, minor-to-moderate):** the document's two bare-field TOC lists (`TOC \\h \\z \\c \"Table\"/\"Figure\"`) sit outside the single gallery SDT, so their 4 entry paragraphs project with `role='body'` (`docx_parse.py:137` only consults `_control_role` for `w:sdt`). Combined with `research_seed.py:139`, a quote from such a TOC entry can be mechanically labeled `project_material` despite the instruction forbidding 目录 as proof. Unconditional PASS requires either extending derived-TOC recognition to bare fields, or the owner explicitly accepting the limitation within the pending human source-review gate.\n\nMinor observations (no action requested): `raw` for source-basis candidates is unverified (only reference quotes are checked); whitespace-only `logical_source_key` surfaces as pydantic ValidationError at service level (API layer blocks it earlier); the archive is opened twice per parse. Limitations: EndNote capability wasn't exercised by MG-K10 itself (verified via the frozen CMS-D008 test, which passed); no UI exists, so frontend checks are contract-level, not browser acceptance.",
